/-!
# Move actual mesh words onto the sewn boundary

Tree sewing gives an executable boundary route for every original triangle
edge. Replacing a sewn edge by the other patch's remaining boundary keeps
the endpoints and an explicit signed sum of face boundaries. No face
integral is assumed to vanish. This is the finite chain comparison, before
any intersection or standard-basis identification.
-/

